  "text": "The taste of sugar is sweet.\n\nTo improve clarity and precision, the modifier \"only\" should be moved to directly precede the noun it modifies. In the original sentence, \"I only have pies for dinner on Thursdays\" is ambiguous because \"only\" could modify \"have,\" \"pies,\" or the entire phrase \"for dinner on Thursdays.\" Placing it before \"pies\" clarifies that pies are the exclusive food item consumed.\n\nRevised sentence: I have only pies for dinner on Thursdays."
